    {
      "id": "2074948137182257284",
      "text": "I've been letting Claude and GLT-5.5 write almost all of my commit messages recently, but I don't feel great about it\n\n\"omitting the higher-level framing needed to understand broadly what the code is doing\" is definitely the key problem there",
      "author": {
        "id": "12497",
        "name": "Simon Willison",
        "screenName": "simonw",
        "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/378800000261649705/be9cc55e64014e6d7663c50d7cb9fc75_normal.jpeg",
        "verified": true
      },
      "metrics": {
        "likes": 456,
        "retweets": 17,
        "replies": 58,
        "quotes": 4,
        "views": 62814,
        "bookmarks": 127
      },
      "createdAt": "Wed Jul 08 20:06:01 +0000 2026",
      "createdAtLocal": "2026-07-08 16:06",
      "createdAtISO": "2026-07-08T20:06:01+00:00",
      "media": [],
      "urls": [],
      "isRetweet": false,
      "retweetedBy": null,
      "lang": "en",
      "score": null,
      "quotedTweet": {
        "id": "2074924213983740233",
        "text": "I just declared a moratorium against AI-written change descriptions (e.g. PR and commit messages, also issues/tickets) from my team.\n\nAI was writing change descriptions that were worse than useless to me as I tried to review PRs: outlining details of the code that could easily be seen by looking at the code, but omitting the higher-level framing needed to understand broadly what the code is doing.\n\nI think people like having AI write these things because the output looks structured and thorough, which makes it feel professional in a way. But this isn't actually valuable. Concise, high-level descriptions are better for everyone. If I need to use my own AI to interpret what your AI wrote then something is wrong. Let AI write code, sure, but for the description, I'd rather see your prompt than your output.\n\nWe could maybe have extended agents.md with guidelines on writing descriptions, but this seemed a bit pointless since a good, concise change description only takes a few minutes to write -- not a significant time savings to delegate to AI. At least, it doesn't take long if you understand the code -- and if you don't understand the code, then I'm definitely not merging it.",
        "author": {
          "screenName": "KentonVarda",
          "name": "Kenton Varda"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2074948354778493232",
      "text": "Sometimes they DO attempt to do that but guess the rationale incorrectly, which is worse than not adding no a rationale at all\n\nI do try to link commits back to issues though, which are written by me and provide a much better answer to the reason behind a change",
      "author": {
        "id": "12497",
        "name": "Simon Willison",
        "screenName": "simonw",
        "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/378800000261649705/be9cc55e64014e6d7663c50d7cb9fc75_normal.jpeg",
        "verified": true
