    {
      "id": "2072730602344984821",
      "text": "I really like this \"understand to participate\" framing of the cognitive debt problem when working with coding agents",
      "author": {
        "id": "12497",
        "name": "Simon Willison",
        "screenName": "simonw",
        "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/378800000261649705/be9cc55e64014e6d7663c50d7cb9fc75_normal.jpeg",
        "verified": true
      },
      "metrics": {
        "likes": 303,
        "retweets": 25,
        "replies": 26,
        "quotes": 2,
        "views": 54411,
        "bookmarks": 200
      },
      "createdAt": "Thu Jul 02 17:14:19 +0000 2026",
      "createdAtLocal": "2026-07-02 13:14",
      "createdAtISO": "2026-07-02T17:14:19+00:00",
      "media": [],
      "urls": [],
      "isRetweet": false,
      "retweetedBy": null,
      "lang": "en",
      "score": null,
      "quotedTweet": {
        "id": "2072522267414901109",
        "text": "That's where another answer comes in: we can understand to participate.\n\nYou can learn what the agent is doing to make sure you can be an active participant in the creative process. Here's why this matters... 7/",
        "author": {
          "screenName": "geoffreylitt",
          "name": "Geoffrey Litt"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2072730868502970642",
      "text": "\"You need a rich set of concepts in your mind to think creatively and fluently about how to move something forward.\"",
      "author": {
        "id": "12497",
        "name": "Simon Willison",
        "screenName": "simonw",
        "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/378800000261649705/be9cc55e64014e6d7663c50d7cb9fc75_normal.jpeg",
        "verified": true
      },
      "metrics": {
        "likes": 35,
        "retweets": 2,
        "replies": 6,
        "quotes": 1,
        "views": 13672,
        "bookmarks": 17
      },
      "createdAt": "Thu Jul 02 17:15:23 +0000 2026",
      "createdAtLocal": "2026-07-02 13:15",
      "createdAtISO": "2026-07-02T17:15:23+00:00",
      "media": [],
      "urls": [],
      "isRetweet": false,
      "retweetedBy": null,
      "lang": "en",
      "score": null,
      "quotedTweet": {
        "id": "2072522270850080968",
        "text": "It's never just one loop! A project is many, many loops with the agent.\n\nAnd the understanding you have of the system is part of your ability to come up with the next idea to evolve it. \n\nYou need a rich set of concepts in your mind to think creatively and fluently about how to move something forward. If you're lacking that fluency, your ability to participate in the project is meaningfully limited. 8/",
        "author": {
          "screenName": "geoffreylitt",
          "name": "Geoffrey Litt"
        }
      }
    },
    {
